From {{der|en|sco|bicker}}, from {{der|en|enm|biker}}. {{doublet|en|beaker}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|Scotland}} A wooden drinking-cup or other [[dish]].
#* '''1824''', {{w|James Hogg}}, ''The Private Memoirs and Confessions of a Justified Sinner'', Oxford 2010, p. 6:
#*: …the liquors were handed around in great fulness, the ale in large wooden '''bickers''', and the brandy in capacious horns of oxen.

